{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310674,"nonce":"jVI/wTCwGwr00lhVdumoPzgz26w=","title":"FIXED bfbe3ffc + 647a7f0b — a trailing comment on a #if line flipped the condition false, and the harness called test methods the entry ...","message":"Two fixes out of the `uncompiled` triage, MEASURED SEPARATELY because only one\nis a compiler fix.\n\n**1. COMPILER, bfbe3ffc: a trailing comment on a `#if` line became part of the\ncondition.** `parser/src/preprocessor.rs` did\n`trimmed.strip_prefix(\"#if \").unwrap().trim()` — the WHOLE rest of the line.\nSo `#if !hl // too many arguments in HL` evaluated FALSE and silently compiled\nthe OTHER branch. Both the stdlib and the Haxe corpus write directives that\nway. Added `condition_text()` (strips `//` and `/*` outside quotes), applied to\n`#if` AND `#elseif`. **506 -\u003e 508, uncompiled 50 -\u003e 46, no regressions.**\nFixture: `haxe-conformance/regressions/PreprocessorComment.hx`.\nPROOF IT IS REAL: `#if !hl` taken, `#if !hl // c` NOT taken, `#if (!hl)` taken.\n\n**2. HARNESS, 647a7f0b — NOT a compiler improvement, say so when quoting the\nnumber.** `haxe-conformance/run.sh` generated `main` by regexing\n`function test*(` across the WHOLE FILE and calling every match as\n`inst.\u003cm\u003e()` on the ENTRY class. A case with a private sibling class /\ninterface / extern that has a `test*` method therefore called a member the\nreceiver does not have — **a program Haxe itself rejects**. rayzor instead\nsynthesises a bodyless member and trap-stubs it, so the row scored as a\ncompiler failure WHILE MEASURING NOTHING. Now scoped to the entry class's own\nbody, and a static is called on the class. **508 -\u003e 517, 9 rows CRASH -\u003e PASS\n(2042 2813 3658 3967 4723 4772 6298 7120 8944).**\n**THE CHECK THAT MATTERS: `scored` stayed 1100 and `skip` stayed 140** — the\ngain is NOT tests dropping out of scoring. Always verify that when touching the\nharness.\n\n**LESSON: some \"compiler failures\" are the measuring instrument.** 9 of the 50\nremaining `uncompiled` rows were harness artifacts. When a cluster resists,\ncheck whether the generated program is even valid Haxe — diff the run dir's\ngenerated file (`$TMPDIR/rayzor_conformance/run/\u003cIssue\u003e/...hx`) against the\ncorpus original.\n\n**STILL OPEN from the same triage** (see\n[[project_uncompiled_cluster_root_census]]):\n- `#if static` is never defined. rayzor masquerades as `eval` for stdlib branch\n  selection (compilation/mod.rs), so adding `static` has stdlib-wide blast\n  radius — NOT a casual change, measure it alone.\n- `@:genericBuild`, `@:using`/`@:resolve` static extensions, member macro\n  functions, `new T()` on a Constructible type param — each 1-2 rows.\n- Filed as git-bug issues: `cast this : Self` in an enum abstract loses the\n  value (f119f71, hits Xml.toString =\u003e 3 rows), array comprehension `if`\n  filter pushes a default (2409b48), Meta.getFields (cee4efc).\n\n- Index summary moved from MEMORY.md (2026-10-18): 506 -\u003e 517. (1) COMPILER bfbe3ffc: a trailing `// comment` on a `#if` line flipped the condition FALSE. (2) HARNESS 647a7f0b, NOT a compiler win: the injected main called `test*` methods the entry class does not have (invalid Haxe). Check `scored`/`skip` are unchanged whenever you touch the harness.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_preprocessor_and_harness_hid_real_rows` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}